---
import PublicLayout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
import Card from '../components/ui/Card.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';
---

<PublicLayout
  title="About — ServiceNow Learn Easy"
  description="Why ServiceNow Learn Easy exists and the teaching approach behind the courses."
>
  <Section
    size="hero"
    headingLevel="h1"
    eyebrow="About"
    title="Practical teaching, without the theatre."
    description="ServiceNow Learn Easy is an independent training project. The goal is simple: explain the platform through the tasks administrators actually perform."
  >
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] lg:items-start">
      <div class="space-y-6 text-body">
        <p>
          Most ServiceNow learning material explains every field on every form. That is useful as a
          reference. It is a poor way to learn a workflow.
        </p>
        <p>
          The courses here start with a task: resolve an incident, route a problem, run a discovery
          schedule, or publish a knowledge article. Each lesson shows the platform behavior that
          makes the task work, then stops.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lessons are short by design. One idea, one demonstration, one result. Progress saves to
          your account so you can continue on another device.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Card tone="wash">
        <p class="text-utility font-medium uppercase text-graphite-copy">Teaching principles</p>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-4">
          <li>
            <h2 class="text-feature-label font-medium">Task before theory</h2>
            <p class="mt-1 text-caption text-graphite-copy">
              Start with the work, then explain why the platform behaves that way.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h2 class="text-feature-label font-medium">One idea per lesson</h2>
            <p class="mt-1 text-caption text-graphite-copy">
              Short lessons are easier to finish and easier to revisit.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h2 class="text-feature-label font-medium">No invented proof</h2>
            <p class="mt-1 text-caption text-graphite-copy">
              No student reviews, completion counts, or credentials are published unless they can be
              verified.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section
    tone="wash"
    eyebrow="Instructor"
    title="Biography pending verification"
    description="This section is intentionally incomplete. Publishing credentials before verification would mislead students."
  >
    <Card>
      <h2 class="text-card-heading">What will appear here</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-body">
        <li>Verified professional background and relevant ServiceNow experience.</li>
        <li>Certifications, with issuing body and validity where applicable.</li>
        <li>Teaching experience and the subjects the instructor can support.</li>
        <li>A direct contact route for course questions.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-caption text-graphite-copy">
        Until this information is verified, treat all instructor content on this site as sample copy
        for review.
      </p>
      <Button href="/contact" variant="secondary" size="sm" class="mt-6">
        Contact page
      </Button>
    </Card>
  </Section>

  <Section
    size="compact"
    align="center"
    title="Review the catalog instead."
    description="Course outlines are sample content. You can review the structure before enrollment opens."
  >
    <div class="flex justify-center">
      <Button href="/courses">Browse courses</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>
</PublicLayout>
